That patch applies to Sentinel (c) 1988 Firebird.

This install has the slave-version 1.01.
It needs WHDLoad v17+ and RawDIC in the path (eg in c:).
To install from a different drive than df0: select
Expert as installation mode.

Fixed:  Disk system of that game is (was) one single great bug.
        Game used odd-adress error, which failed on 68020+.
        Keyboard interrupt.

V1.01 (15.09.2017) done by StingRay:
- Blitter wait added to avoid graphics corruption (Mantis #1942),
  blitter wait patch can be disabled with CUSTOM1
- RawDIC imager added
- Interrupt fixed
- Default quitkey changed to F10
- Source code included
- Install script updated


Notes:  The icon is a dual romicon/newicon.
        Lets fast remember the keys: a-absorb, sdl,u-movement,
          h-end/fail level, btr-build, q-quit body, <esc>-quit level,
          <cursor left/down>-(un)pause, <f2><f3>-toggle music/sound,
          <space bar>-switch input mode.

Default quitkey is F10. Change it with the QUITKEY-tooltype.

The install is tested with 2 MB on an A1200, and on an 18 MB 68030.

Disclaimer: Although i try to make my installs as reliable as possible, you 
          use them wholly on your own risk.

Full whdload package:	aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?.lha
Other installs:		http://www.fh-zwickau.de/~jah/whdload/
Report bugs with the bug report form on that page.

Harry in October 1998.
